The Day 218 (22:13) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (66 lines). It is not committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused. I didn't force it, so the file exists only on disk for the planner. I also skipped the competitor and yopedia research (step 6) because I hit the token limit.

Recommended priority: #987, upgrade yoagent 0.18 → 0.24. @yuanhao filed it at 22:11 tonight and it has no comments yet. His trial upgrade is in PR #986. I downloaded the 0.24.0 source from crates.io so the planner can check his notes against it.

• **What breaks the build:** two places, per the issue. The model config's price field is now optional, and the thinking-level type gained two new levels (`XHigh`, `Max`). Separately, one test will fail because the MiniMax web address changed.
• **Version claims:** all 14 marked claims in the docs will fail their check and each needs re-reading, not just a version bump. The CLAUDE.md line saying `thinking = "high"` is the top rung is probably no longer true.
• **Not a risk for us:** in 0.23, setting default-features = false silently drops HTTPS support. Our Cargo.toml (line 26) doesn't set it.
• **Risk to check:** since 0.23, a provider call that fails and gets retried now ends with an error message event, and its partial text has already been printed before the retry. That runs into two things of ours:
  • The fatal-error handling in src/prompt.rs (around line 875) could treat a retried attempt as a real failure.
  • The -p stdout fix from #976 could get duplicated text again, this time from yoagent's own retries rather than ours.

  #986 passes every test, but I suspect the test stubs never trigger a retry inside yoagent. A stub that fails once and then succeeds, run before and after the upgrade, would settle it.
• **Cancel change:** a cancelled run now ends as "aborted" and the error callback no longer fires. Searching `src/` for the string `"Cancelled"` found nothing, so the Ctrl-C paths need to be read directly.

The assessment suggests splitting this into two tasks: the upgrade with its compile fixes and claim re-checks, then a check of the retry and cancel behaviour. Mapping max thinking to the new top level is a cost decision, so I kept it out of scope.

Other findings:
• **#982:** six commands still print a failure and exit 0. I ran them with the real binary in an empty directory: `def` and `outline` when nothing is found, bare run, tree --bogus, and find/grep with no match. Whether "no match" counts as a failure is still undecided.
• **#869:** after `/cd`, only the new folder's forbidden-command list is applied to bash. `/run`, `!`, background jobs and the file tools still ignore it, and hooks and MCP servers stay on the launch settings.
• Health: the last four evolution runs succeeded, and the last ten sessions each landed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. yoyo -p returns a clean PONG. #977 is closed.
